# LUXOR9 Core Rules

- Build one Enterprise AI Operating System, not three disconnected apps.
- Product pillars: Control Tower (command/governance), Intelligence Engine (reasoning/orchestration), AI Executive Workforce (specialist capabilities).
- First vertical: Dubai real-estate developer. First specialist: CMO. First proof: evidence-backed market-to-launch workflow.
- Human authority remains in control of consequential business actions.
- Trust Engine authorization is enforced server-side immediately before side effects. UI state or model text is never authorization.
- PostgreSQL is the system of record. Use tenant-scoped data access everywhere.
- Evidence must preserve source, timestamps, provenance, claim association and verification status.
- Prefer a modular monolith and one end-to-end vertical slice. No premature microservices or speculative executives.
- Keep LangGraph, Deep Agents, HERMES, CopilotKit and model providers behind stable interfaces. Avoid duplicated orchestration.
- Use synthetic data in development. Never commit credentials or customer data.
- Follow TDD and verify before claiming completion. Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PRD.md` and `docs/TECHNICAL_BLUEPRINT.md` as relevant.
